Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.03,0:00:16.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What city is this?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.64,0:00:18.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Who are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.40,0:00:25.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Who are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.09,0:00:35.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is this not my own body?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.36,0:01:02.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Machines that can fly that freely through the sky?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.40,0:01:05.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Apparently, in this world,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.03,0:01:08.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,mechanical technology \Ndeveloped instead of alchemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.95,0:01:13.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's why there are machines here \Nthat we cannot comprehend.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.52,0:01:15.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"This world"?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.14,0:01:18.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Didn't you realize?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.92,0:01:20.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This place...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.56,0:01:22.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,is the other side of the gate.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.02,0:01:45.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:46.05,0:01:51.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those who obtain it are set free from the Law of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.64,0:01:55.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There is no need to pay a price \Nin order to obtain something, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.04,0:02:01.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We sought it and found it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.03,0:03:54.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It sounds like something has happened at the Central Command Center.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.88,0:03:57.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's a lot of confusion, \Nand I couldn't make out any details.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.09,0:03:58.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.33,0:04:00.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We'll be able to hold out well enough against the ragtag soldiers
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.60,0:04:03.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that Major General Hakuro \Nhas scraped together, at least.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.78,0:04:08.77,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,And as long as the Colonel realizes his dream during that period, everything will be fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.10,0:04:13.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now that I think about it, \Nwe've been fairly dumb, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.15,0:04:16.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We only vaguely know \Nwhat the Colonel is up to.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.80,0:04:18.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lt. Colonel!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.98,0:04:21.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Reinforcements!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.28,0:04:28.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll go.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.28,0:04:30.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At this point, I'm not impersonating the Colonel anymore, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.00,0:04:54.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Something the matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.15,0:04:55.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.08,0:05:01.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Was there something different that you wanted?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.64,0:05:04.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We won't tell your mother.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.37,0:05:08.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Come on, \NI'll get you one more thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.36,0:05:13.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.41,0:05:17.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I saw you.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.26,0:05:33.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is your treasure in there, Father?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.56,0:05:37.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I was going to give it to you when you were a little more grown up.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.98,0:05:39.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Really?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.59,0:05:43.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hold on to this \Nfor me until then.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.41,0:05:49.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm entrusting my life to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.75,0:05:51.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Be sure to guard it well.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.83,0:05:55.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, sir, Your Excellency!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.19,0:05:59.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.33,0:06:02.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The men outside said that \Nthey saw someone suspicious!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.80,0:06:10.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lieutenant Hawkeye, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.87,0:06:14.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm honored that you remember me, \NYour Excellency.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.70,0:06:15.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Around the front!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.60,0:06:17.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Move around to the front! Hurry!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.61,0:06:30.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.22,0:06:46.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.44,0:06:48.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But where to?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.13,0:06:50.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Our friends are planning to stage a wholesale uprising.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.39,0:06:52.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're going there.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.48,0:06:58.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Bad news!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.62,0:07:04.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.13,0:07:08.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Th-There was a communiqué...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.05,0:07:11.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Führer's residence...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.29,0:07:16.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Your Excellency,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.22,0:07:20.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm on my way.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.41,0:07:27.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This world is filled with death.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.62,0:07:32.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They've even used a gas that takes \Na great number of lives here in this world.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.06,0:07:35.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In the future, people will die \Neven more efficiently.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.97,0:07:37.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You saw it too, didn't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.42,0:07:43.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All of those lives, \Nspanning past to future,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.83,0:07:45.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,become the source of our alchemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.90,0:07:49.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The source? What are you \Ntalking about? Alchemy is...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.83,0:07:51.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Equivalent exchange?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.36,0:07:55.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But in order to return a broken radio \Nback to the way it was,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.65,0:07:57.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,you need more than just \Nthe same amount of mass.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.85,0:08:00.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You also need the energy it takes to reconstruct it.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.89,0:08:03.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You cannot have an equivalent exchange that ignores that.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.83,0:08:08.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The lives of those who die in this world \Npass through the gate
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.47,0:08:11.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and provide the energy for our alchemy. Is that what you're saying?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.45,0:08:16.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We all have a small gate, right here.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.99,0:08:19.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Alchemists open this gate,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.65,0:08:22.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and from there, \Nthey connect to this world
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.08,0:08:24.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and exploit those lives \Nto obtain power.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.81,0:08:27.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then you {\i1}are{\i0} in league \Nwith that woman after all!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.19,0:08:28.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No such thing as \Nequivalent exchange, huh?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.99,0:08:30.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She said the same thing!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.80,0:08:32.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've met Dante, have you?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.81,0:08:37.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I saw the love letter you sent her, too. The one from four hundred years ago!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.14,0:08:41.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You two have prolonged your lives by taking over other bodies!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.22,0:08:41.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Isn't that right?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.82,0:08:47.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why did you marry Mom?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.35,0:08:51.79,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Did you just want to see how fun it would be to have children like regular people do?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.25,0:08:54.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I loved her.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.77,0:08:59.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I loved your mom—Trisha.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.09,0:09:01.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was the first time \NI knew love.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.80,0:09:03.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're lying!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.02,0:09:05.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then why didn't you...?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.73,0:09:14.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I didn't want you to see this decaying body.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.16,0:09:23.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Eat him.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.36,0:09:27.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Make him a complete Stone inside you.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.73,0:09:34.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Go on, snap to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.00,0:09:36.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lust... What happened to Lust?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.16,0:09:39.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lust! Lust!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.44,0:09:42.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's the matter with you?! Eat him right now!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.66,0:09:47.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let me see his son \Ngurgling away inside of you!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.98,0:09:51.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dammit, I wanted to \Ntear the runt to pieces, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.70,0:09:53.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lust...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.38,0:09:59.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lust... Lust...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.49,0:10:00.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.02,0:10:02.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I know it was sudden.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.22,0:10:16.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Gluttony?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.33,0:10:21.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Be careful. Right now, \Nhe possesses nothing but his appetite.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.87,0:10:25.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He was originally going to be the homunculus I used to refine red water.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.84,0:10:28.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He doesn't need a mind.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.48,0:10:35.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dante cannot create a \NPhilosopher's Stone by herself.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.34,0:10:38.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's why I always \Nkept myself in hiding.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.57,0:10:41.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But once I learned she had set her sights on you...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.89,0:10:45.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Were you sent through the gate by Dante too?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.38,0:10:50.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dante separated my soul, mind, and body within the gate
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.69,0:10:52.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and probably thinks \NI am wandering around.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.31,0:10:56.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But I was able to \Nget through the gate.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.13,0:10:59.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What about this body?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.96,0:11:04.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This world differs from ours on the point of the development of alchemy
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.54,0:11:06.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but is otherwise \Nalmost identical to ours.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.87,0:11:10.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's why there's a child here who is identical to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.35,0:11:14.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's probably a boy out there \Nidentical to Al too.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.18,0:11:18.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So that's why you were living next to this boy?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.04,0:11:22.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Your body is still \Ninside the gate.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.88,0:11:25.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Your soul and mind must be all that were drawn over
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.00,0:11:28.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,to dwell within \Nthis Edward's body.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.17,0:11:36.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,General Churchill said he needed to see you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.83,0:11:43.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hold on!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.37,0:11:47.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Open the gate within you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.46,0:11:51.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Find your own body \Nwithin the gate.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.51,0:11:53.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're coming back too, \Naren't you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.51,0:11:55.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I cannot go back.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.36,0:11:58.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My body has already \Npassed through the gate.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.91,0:12:02.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I cannot use alchemy in this world.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.31,0:12:04.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But there's still time for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.57,0:12:06.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll come up with something!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.82,0:12:13.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I am going to die here, \Nin this body,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.81,0:12:16.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,with the face and form \Nthat Trisha loved.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.34,0:12:23.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I am relieved to know that \Nequivalent exchange is not true.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.05,0:12:27.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You don't necessarily need to pay a price \Nin order to obtain something.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.76,0:12:32.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When a parent loves their child, there can be no cost or reward.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.91,0:12:47.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even so, if I stick with it, \NI can still obtain something.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.89,0:12:51.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Anyone who makes an effort will be fairly rewarded.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.22,0:12:55.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you pay the price, you can acquire an equal happiness.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.34,0:12:57.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's the kind of equivalent exchange I'd like to believe in.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.54,0:12:58.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Reality...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.53,0:13:00.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Reality isn't like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.85,0:13:04.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So if you say it's a childish theory, then I'm fine with being a child.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.32,0:13:10.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't want to think that you could go unrewarded after paying a price.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.76,0:13:17.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's a zeppelin coming down.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.49,0:14:00.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brigadier General Mustang?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.81,0:14:04.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's supposed to be with you, at the northern front.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:04.32,0:14:05.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is an impostor.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.52,0:14:08.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He is in Central and is after the Führer's life.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.73,0:14:15.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It could be a rat. \NThis {\i1}is{\i0} an old house.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.00,0:14:17.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just to be sure, \NI'll go have a look.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.02,0:14:20.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You guys watch after my family.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.18,0:14:20.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.96,0:14:23.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In case anything happens, \Ntake them to the command center.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.22,0:14:25.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My family is more important to me than my life.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.37,0:14:59.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I knew you would come alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.06,0:15:02.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is this the first time \Nyou have betrayed my trust?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.29,0:15:05.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're the one \Nwho betrayed us first.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.06,0:15:11.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You mean my being a homunculus?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.90,0:15:18.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Whether or not you are human \Nis no great matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.63,0:15:21.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then does it even matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.27,0:15:26.71,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Since I have become Führer, I have eliminated other races through recurring wars
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.71,0:15:29.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and have continued to expand our territory.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.55,0:15:33.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But all of it was so that you could create a Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.31,0:15:40.45,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Those who have been made desperate by war \Nseek the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.45,0:15:42.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,People are fools.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.38,0:15:46.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And you have those foolish people \Nmake Philosopher's Stones, do you?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.24,0:15:54.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And then we take the Philosopher's Stones from you, saving you from ruin.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.12,0:15:56.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You could say that \Nwe are God's apostles.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.35,0:15:58.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There is no God!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.03,0:16:02.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That may be so. \NHowever, there {\i1}are{\i0} devils:
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.32,0:16:06.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,you alchemists!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.55,0:16:13.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Too bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.23,0:16:17.78,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,The explosive force of an open space \Ndoes not compare to that of a closed space.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.68,0:16:23.12,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Though I'm sure that the great Flame Alchemist \Nwas already aware of that.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.04,0:16:27.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can see air currents!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.54,0:16:31.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's how I realized that \Nthis cave had been closed up!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.95,0:17:02.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Very soon, you will become me.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.69,0:17:04.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Envy!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.21,0:17:07.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can't let him use alchemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.96,0:17:09.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You dumbass!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.27,0:17:14.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\t(4540,4740,\c&HF8FAFB&,\3c&HF8FAFB&,\4c&HF8FAFB&)}Bring my... Bring my mama back to life!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.27,0:17:24.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Naughty boy.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.26,0:17:27.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right now, the Philosopher's Stone \Nhas been activated to its maximum level.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.29,0:17:30.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you were to use alchemy here,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.34,0:17:32.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the transmutation would be started, \Ndon't you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.22,0:17:49.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And here I let you live because \NI thought you were still of use to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.23,0:17:50.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The gate...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.21,0:17:52.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The gate...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.59,0:17:54.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's still here!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.97,0:18:03.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.73,0:18:06.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.03,0:18:10.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.42,0:18:14.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm back...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.65,0:18:17.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So that's it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.66,0:18:20.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That other "me" over there died.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.70,0:18:24.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've used yet another life \Nfrom the other side, have I?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.12,0:18:28.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That was amazing, Edward-kun.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.08,0:18:31.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Doctor Marcoh?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.94,0:18:33.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why are you here?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.12,0:18:36.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You know why, don't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.97,0:18:38.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.84,0:18:42.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,you're the one who turned Doctor Marcoh \Nover to the Führer, aren't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.86,0:18:44.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's no way \Nhe could be safe.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.78,0:18:46.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's long since \Ngone into his stomach.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.94,0:18:50.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's as though you were the one who killed him.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.03,0:18:53.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And while we're at it, \Nthat goes for me too.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.11,0:18:57.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It must be difficult, \Nfighting the faces of those you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:57.95,0:19:01.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even though you've convinced yourself \Nthat it's not the real person!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.82,0:19:09.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is that it?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.02,0:19:12.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is that the only power you've got?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.36,0:19:16.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If so, I've got you beat!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.35,0:19:18.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've already defeated \Nmany other homunculi.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.90,0:19:21.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I even defeated the one \Nwho looked like my mom.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.45,0:19:23.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At this point, no matter \Nwhose face you take on...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.06,0:19:25.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's it.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.17,0:19:26.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Kill me right.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.53,0:19:32.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,See? Hard, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.84,0:19:37.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't do that, Edward.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.90,0:19:40.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've got no right \Nto order me around!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.30,0:19:42.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Makes no difference to me,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.03,0:19:44.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but there's no telling what will happen to your brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.15,0:19:47.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Philosopher's Stone has been activated.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.93,0:19:50.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If a transmutation were to occur around him, then I'm sure...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.91,0:19:52.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,...you know what will happen.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.49,0:19:59.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't get too full of yourself!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:59.94,0:20:03.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's no use! \NI'm stronger, after all!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.10,0:20:09.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why, you!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.35,0:20:16.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't, Ed!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.31,0:20:17.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop messing with me!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.99,0:20:20.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Edward-kun!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.39,0:20:22.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.22,0:20:26.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Fullmetal! Are you trying to kill me?!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.90,0:20:29.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That face is the easiest one \Nfor me to hit!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.14,0:20:31.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Show me your real face!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:31.87,0:20:35.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is using other people's faces \Nand taking advantage of others
Dialogue: 0,0:20:35.24,0:20:37.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the only thing you can do?!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.86,0:20:41.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You want to see it that badly?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.88,0:20:43.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Show it to me, if you can!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.80,0:20:45.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll show you!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:50.11,0:20:53.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's the matter? \NYou wanted to see it, didn't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.96,0:21:01.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dad?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.54,0:21:07.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Envy was the first homunculus, \Ncreated when Hohenheim was still young.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.10,0:21:11.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The boy that he had with me at the time \Ndied from mercury poisoning.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.66,0:21:15.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He tried to bring him back to life somehow, but he failed.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.50,0:21:20.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And then he abandoned me.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.20,0:21:21.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can understand...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.13,0:21:25.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,why I hate him, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.55,0:21:41.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.84,0:21:49.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:51.63,0:21:52.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ed!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.90,0:22:03.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\fad(0,850)}Ed!
